# Added 2026-09-07 after the laptop checkout turned three committed cron
# wrappers into CRLF. These files RUN ON LINUX (VPS cron): a `\r` at end of
# line gives "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M" or silently mangles arguments, so
# a CRLF commit would have killed the national-landscape, matchup-card and
# team-card crons the next time the VPS pulled.
#
# Scoped to .sh/.py ON PURPOSE — a blanket `* text=auto` would renormalise the
# ~35 perpetually-modified config JSONs in one enormous commit.
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.py  text eol=lf
